\title{A 1.5\,V, 50\,mA PMOS LDO in SkyWater sky130:\\ schematic, layout and sign-off with the open PDK decks}
\author{Vu-Quoc-Minh Nguyen}
\date{@@DATE@@}

\begin{document}
\maketitle

\begin{abstract}
\noindent A low-dropout regulator ($\VIN = 1.8$\,V, $\VOUT = 1.5$\,V, $\IL$ up to 50\,mA, $C_L = 2.2\,\mu$F) is designed in SkyWater sky130 with the 1.8\,V devices, laid out in Electric by a script, and checked with the official open-source decks of the PDK: KLayout DRC (\texttt{sky130A\_mr.drc}: @@DRC_N@@ violations) and KLayout LVS (\texttt{sky130.lvs}: netlists match, including the poly resistors). Current densities are checked against the limits of the SkyWater technology LEF; the first layout failed them and the power routing was redone. Parasitics are extracted with KLayout-PEX (2.5D engine, RC) and the performance is simulated again on the extracted netlist. All numbers in this report are produced by the scripts of the repository.
\end{abstract}

