\section{Layout}

The layout is generated by \texttt{layout/gen\_layout.py} in Electric 9.08 (built-in \texttt{skywater130} technology) and exported to GDS; \texttt{layout/postproc.py} then adds the two things Electric does not write: the \texttt{poly\_rs} marker (66/13) on the resistor bodies, without which the decks see no precision resistor, and the pin labels (70/5). Size $\approx @@AREA@@$.

\begin{figure}[H]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{../figures/layout_full.png}
\caption{\texttt{ldo\_final.gds} (KLayout, sky130 layer colours). Left to right: divider (6 units + 2 dummies), NMOS row ($M_{BN}$, $M_T$, $M_1$, $M_2$, $M_{CS}$) with the met3 signal tracks above it, PMOS row ($M_3$, $M_4$, $M_{BL}$, $M_D$) in the n-well, and the pass device (4 columns $\times$ 40 fingers) under the power plates.}
\label{fig:layout}
\end{figure}

\paragraph{Power path.} The pass device carries the whole load current. Its drain and source rows are joined by vertical met2 straps (three of each per column). In the first layout the straps ended on a met3 rail of 1\,$\mu$m (vout) or 2\,$\mu$m (vin) width, and the vin pin sat 45\,$\mu$m away from the array; 50\,mA in these rails is 50 and 25\,mA/$\mu$m, far above the met3 limit of 6.8\,mA/$\mu$m (Sec.~\ref{sec:em}). The final layout covers the array with two met3 + met4 plates, vout over the lower half and vin over the upper half (about 9.4\,$\mu$m tall each). Every drain (source) row inside the vout (vin) plate has a via2 of $3\times2$ cuts from its strap, the two plate layers are joined by @@VIA3@@ via3 cuts each, and the vin and vout pins are at the plate centres.

\begin{figure}[H]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=0.48\linewidth]{../figures/layout_pass_zoom.png}
\caption{One pass column and a half: the via2 stacks on the drain straps (lower half, vout plate) and on the source straps (upper half, vin plate), and the via3 arrays.}
\end{figure}

\section{Physical verification}

\subsection{DRC}
Deck: \texttt{sky130A\_mr.drc} (efabless, release 2024.2.11\_01.09), KLayout 0.30.12, front end, back end and off-grid checks. Result on \texttt{ldo\_final.gds}: \textbf{@@DRC_N@@ violations}. The first run had nine: eight \texttt{licon.1} (the 0.19$\times$2.0\,$\mu$m contact slots of the resistors, exempt only when \texttt{poly\_rs} is present, which Electric had not written) and one \texttt{m3.6} (a 0.16\,$\mu$m$^2$ met3 pad in a via stack, now 0.36\,$\mu$m$^2$). Electric's own DRC still lists errors (psdm spacing between overlapping implant shapes, poly-to-diffusion spacing, and met3 spacing where the plates overlap wires that Electric treats as other nodes); the official deck reports none of them.

\subsection{LVS}
Deck: \texttt{sky130.lvs} (efabless \texttt{sky130\_klayout\_pdk}, commit 13d25721), against a CDL netlist written from \texttt{sizes.json} (\texttt{scripts/ldo\_cdl.py}). Result: \textbf{netlists match}. After the deck combines the fingers and the series resistor units, the extracted netlist is:

