device & model & $W$ ($\mu$m) & $L$ ($\mu$m) / $R$ \\
\midrule
@@LVS_ROWS@@
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

\noindent To check that the flow can fail, the comparison was repeated with four deliberately wrong netlists (\texttt{layout/lvs\_negative\_test.py}): 150 instead of 160 pass fingers, $M_2$'s gate on $V_{REF}$, one resistor unit 5\,$\mu$m long, $L(M_{CS}) = 0.6\,\mu$m. All four were reported as mismatches, the correct netlist as a match.

\subsection{Electromigration}\label{sec:em}
Limits: the SkyWater technology LEF \texttt{sky130\_fd\_sc\_hd.tlef} (average DC current, junction temperature 90\,\textdegree C): 2.8\,mA/$\mu$m (met1, met2), 6.8\,mA/$\mu$m (met3, met4), and per cut 0.36 (mcon), 0.29 (via), 0.48 (via2, via3)\,mA. The check (\texttt{layout/em\_check.py}) measures widths and cut counts on the GDS and assumes the worst case for each element: the whole current that a branch can carry passes through its narrowest element, with no sharing. At $\IL = 50$\,mA each of the 160 fingers carries 0.31\,mA.

\begin{table}[H]
\centering\small
\caption{EM check of the pass-device path at 50\,mA, worst-case bounds.}
\begin{tabular}{lrrl}
\toprule
element & $I$ (mA) & limit (mA) & measured \\
\midrule
@@EM_ROWS@@
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

\noindent Every element is within its limit. The closest are the met1 bar of a contact row (0.625 of 0.728\,mA, with all of the row's current assumed to leave on one side) and the plate via2 (@@EM_VIA2@@). The limits are for 90\,\textdegree C; at the 125\,\textdegree C corner they are lower, and this was not checked.

\section{Parasitic extraction and post-layout simulation}

\paragraph{Extraction.} KLayout-PEX 0.8.1, 2.5D analytical engine, mode RC, sky130A technology data of the tool. The raw netlist has @@PEX_R_FULL@@ resistors and @@PEX_C_FULL@@ capacitors. ngspice needs about ten minutes for one operating point of it; the netlist was therefore reduced with the TICER pass of the same tool (time-constant threshold 10\,ps, i.e.\ an error per eliminated node of about $2\pi f\tau = 6\times10^{-5}$ at 1\,MHz, exact at DC) to @@PEX_R@@ resistors and @@PEX_C@@ capacitors. The full and the reduced netlist give the same operating point ($\VOUT$ = 1.50085\,V, supply current 164.303\,$\mu$A at 0.1\,mA load). The DC sweeps (load and line regulation, dropout, quiescent current) use the same netlist without its capacitors, which do not enter a DC solution; the AC and transient runs use the full reduced RC netlist. The substrate node of the extraction is tied to ground; the 2.5D engine has no substrate resistance. For the loop gain, the gate of $M_2$ is cut from the feedback net in the extracted netlist and the loop is broken there, as in the schematic.

